<title>CHILE: Chile's Masisa ups Argentine unit capital.</title>
<headline>Chile's Masisa ups Argentine unit capital.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean forestry company Maderas y Sinteticos SA (Masisa) said it increased the capital of its Argentine division by $11 million.</p>
<p>The company offered shares, all of which were sold to outside parties, said Masisa in a statement.</p>
<p>The company, Chile's largest board producer, did not say how its planned to invest the funds raised by the capital increase.</p>
<p>Masisa produces particle boards, wood doors and lumber.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
</text>
